/// The mirrors' module: `ObjectMirror` and `ClassMirror`, through which a
/// program reads the structure of its objects and classes, reached
/// through `platform mirrors`, and the other mirrors a program reaches
/// only by navigating from those two. Built on its first demand, or by
/// the loader when an image names it, over
/// the VM mirror and the kernel, from which it takes `Error` and
/// `ArgumentError`.
///
/// The factory pattern `PlatformFactory.ns` is written in: this root holds
/// the VM mirror, which the platform's root hands it, and of the kernel only
/// the two classes it needs, never the kernel instance; nothing hands
/// its instance to a program. The platform's root builds it through the
/// mirror on its first use -- again after an unwind interrupted that use,
/// which records nothing -- and keeps it in a private lazy slot,
/// and each platform's `mirrors` getter sends it `build`, its one
/// public member. What a program gets is the `Mirrors` facet `build`
/// answers, which hands out two of this module's private classes,
/// `ObjectMirror` and `ClassMirror`, by class accessors, each exactly
/// `^outer MirrorsFactory <Name>` -- a lexical
/// send, which lets an image name the class by its declaration
/// (`docs/design/image-format.md`, "Shipped names"). Its nested classes
/// reach the mirror lexically, as members of this root, never through a
/// slot of their own. Nothing a program can name answers this root's
/// instance or its class, so no program can build one over something that
/// is not the mirror. Keep it so: no code whose receiver is this root's
/// instance may send it anything it does not understand, since a
/// `MessageNotUnderstood` hands its receiver to whoever catches it.
///
/// The shipped-level rule, which every refusal below follows: a mirror
/// hands out a value only through a level whose mixin is not shipped. A
/// slot a core-library mixin declares is neither read by `getSlot:` nor
/// listed by `slots`; the enclosing object of a core-library class is not
/// reflected; and a class mirror reached by navigation -- an object's
/// class, a superclass -- does not hand out a core-library class, which a
/// program that can name the class gets back from the mirror it made
/// itself with `ClassMirror reflecting:`. What stays readable of a
/// core-library class is its structure: names, selectors, access
/// modifiers, slot declarations and the superclass chain as further
/// mirrors. Otherwise a mirror would hand a program the VM mirror, which
/// a shipped module's root holds, or a shipped module's root itself, a
/// core-library class's enclosing object. The leaves refuse the VM mirror
/// and every shipped module instance whatever the level, behind this
/// rule.
///
/// Mirrors read private and protected members alike: holding the
/// capability, `platform mirrors`, is the access check.
///
/// The factory's parameters are copied into slots because neither a lazy
/// slot nor a method may name them (§6). A send to `vmMirror` here is a
/// mirror send, as in `Kernel.ns`: this module is resolved with
/// `resolve_kernel`, which only shipped source is.
///
/// A value (§3.1.1), so that every platform shares the one module and its
/// classes -- `platform mirrors ClassMirror` is one class however many
/// platforms a program makes; a mirror holds what it reflects, so it is
/// an object.
///
/// @factory makes the mirrors module over `mirror` and `kernel`, copying
/// the mirror into `vmMirror` and the kernel's `Error` and `ArgumentError`
/// into slots of their own and keeping nothing else of the kernel. The
/// platform's root sends it to the class the mirror answers on the module's
/// first demand, and again on the next demand after an unwind interrupted
/// one, which records nothing; the loader sends it instead when an image
/// names the module.
/// @param mirror the VM mirror, through which every mirror reads what it
/// reflects; a mirror sends its reflectee nothing, and forces no future it
/// is given.
/// @param kernel the kernel module instance; its `Error` is what a mirror
/// signals for what it may not read, its `ArgumentError` what
/// `ClassMirror reflecting:` signals for anything that is no class.
class MirrorsFactory usingVmMirror: mirror kernel: kernel = Value (
  |
    /// The VM mirror the factory was given: the one object through which
    /// a mirror reads what it reflects. Never handed out.
    private vmMirror = mirror.
    /// The kernel's `Error`, which a mirror signals for what the
    /// shipped-level rule keeps it from reading.
    private Error = kernel Error.
    /// The kernel's `ArgumentError`, which `ClassMirror reflecting:`
    /// signals for anything that is no class or metaclass.
    private ArgumentError = kernel ArgumentError.
  |
) (
  /// `platform mirrors`: the namespace of the two classes a program
  /// makes mirrors with, `ObjectMirror` and `ClassMirror`, one accessor
  /// each; nothing else. Its own class is not among them, so a program makes no
  /// second namespace.
  private class Mirrors = Value () (
    /// Hands out the class a program makes object mirrors with: it
    /// instantiates it with `reflecting:` any object.
    ///
    /// @answers this module's class `ObjectMirror`.
    public ObjectMirror = (
      ^outer MirrorsFactory ObjectMirror.
    )

    /// Hands out the class a program makes class mirrors with: it
    /// instantiates it with `reflecting:` a class or a metaclass.
    ///
    /// @answers this module's class `ClassMirror`.
    public ClassMirror = (
      ^outer MirrorsFactory ClassMirror.
    )
  )

  /// A mirror on one object: its class, as a class mirror, and the values
  /// of its slots. It sends the object nothing -- its class, its equality
  /// and its hash are asked of the VM -- so an object that overrides `=`,
  /// `hash` or `class`, or a proxy, reflects as itself. A future is such
  /// a proxy: the mirror reflects the future, never the value it stands
  /// for, and never forces it.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror on `anObject`, which it keeps as its
  /// `reflectee` and sends nothing.
  /// @param anObject any object.
  private class ObjectMirror reflecting: anObject = Object (
    |
      /// The object the mirror reflects, as `reflecting:` was given it.
      /// Public, so a program reads back the object it gave, or the one a
      /// navigation reached: a slot's value or an enclosing object.
      public reflectee = anObject.
    |
  ) (
    /// Identifies the receiver as an object mirror, without a class test;
    /// `=` sends it to the object it compares the receiver with.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfObjectMirror = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Reflects the reflectee's class, read through the VM rather than by
    /// sending `class`. The mirror was reached by navigation, so its
    /// `reflectee` hands out the class only when the class is the
    /// program's own (the module's shipped-level rule).
    ///
    /// @answers a new class mirror on the reflectee's class.
    public getClass = (
      ^NavigatedClassMirror anchor: reflectee classFirst: true steps: 0.
    )

    /// Reads the reflectee's slot named `aSymbol`: the slot its own code
    /// sees under that name, which the nearest level of its class
    /// declaring the name declares, never a farther slot that one shadows.
    ///
    /// @param aSymbol a Symbol, the slot's name.
    /// @answers the value of that slot.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `aSymbol`, 'getSlot: requires a
    /// Symbol', when it is no Symbol.
    /// @signals Error 'getSlot: no slot named <name> that a mirror may
    /// read', when the name names no slot a mirror may read: no level
    /// declares it, its nearest declaration is lazy or a core-library
    /// mixin's (the module's shipped-level rule), or the slot holds what no
    /// mirror hands out.
    public getSlot: aSymbol = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionSlotOf: reflectee named: aSymbol ifFail: [^self refuseSlotNamed: aSymbol].
    )

    /// Signals what `getSlot:` signals for a slot it may not read. It never
    /// returns: an Error is not resumable.
    ///
    /// The name's text is read through the VM, which reads only a Symbol,
    /// so that refusing runs no code of the program's.
    ///
    /// @param aName the name `getSlot:` was given.
    /// @answers nothing; it never returns.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `aName`, 'getSlot: requires a
    /// Symbol', when it is no Symbol.
    /// @signals Error 'getSlot: no slot named <name> that a mirror may
    /// read', for a Symbol.
    /// @see `getSlot:`.
    private refuseSlotNamed: aName = (
      |
        text = vmMirror reflectionSymbolText: aName ifFail: [
          ^(ArgumentError value: aName) signal: 'getSlot: requires a Symbol'.
        ].
      |
      ^Error signal: 'getSlot: no slot named ' , text , ' that a mirror may read'.
    )

    /// Lists the reflectee's slots a mirror may read, each the slot
    /// `getSlot:` reads: superclass level first, each level's slots in
    /// declaration order, a name standing where the level declaring its
    /// visible slot puts it. A name whose nearest declaration is lazy or a
    /// core-library mixin's (the module's shipped-level rule) is left out,
    /// as are the indexed elements of an Array or a String; an object with
    /// no such slot answers an empty group.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of SlotMirrors, one per name under which
    /// the reflectee has a slot a mirror may read.
    public slots = (
      |
        names = vmMirror reflectionSlotNamesOf: reflectee ifFail: [{}].
        result ::= {}.
      |
      names do: [:slotName |
        |
          readable ::= true.
          slotValue = vmMirror reflectionSlotOf: reflectee named: slotName ifFail: [
            readable:: false.
          ].
        |
        readable ifTrue: [result:: result , {SlotMirror name: slotName value: slotValue}].
      ].
      ^MirrorGroup over: result.
    )

    /// Compares the receiver with `other` by the identity of their
    /// reflectees: two mirrors on two distinct objects are never equal,
    /// however equal the objects are.
    ///
    /// @param other any object; sent `isKindOfObjectMirror`, and
    /// `reflectee` when it answers true.
    /// @answers whether `other` is an object mirror on the reflectee
    /// itself, a Boolean.
    public = other = (
      other isKindOfObjectMirror ifFalse: [^false].
      ^vmMirror reflectionObject: reflectee identicalTo: other reflectee ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Hashes the receiver by its reflectee's identity, so that two
    /// mirrors on the one object hash alike.
    ///
    /// @answers the reflectee's identity hash.
    public hash = (
      ^vmMirror objectHash: reflectee ifFail: [0].
    )
  )

  /// What every class mirror is: a mirror on one class or metaclass, its
  /// name, its mixin, its superclass chain, its enclosing object and the
  /// slots, methods and nested classes it has, the inherited ones
  /// included, superclass first, the level a `<:` clause adds where it
  /// stands in the chain. Everything is read through the VM; the class is
  /// sent nothing. Never instantiated itself: `ClassMirror` is the mirror
  /// a program makes, `NavigatedClassMirror` the one navigation answers.
  ///
  /// A class mirror holds the way to its class rather than the class: an
  /// anchor -- the class `ClassMirror reflecting:` was given, or the
  /// object whose class an object mirror's `getClass` reflects -- and the
  /// steps from it, recomputed through the VM on every use. A program
  /// holding a mirror reached by navigation so holds only what it gave,
  /// never the core-library class the mirror reflects, which an image
  /// could not name where a program keeps it
  /// (`docs/design/image-format.md`, "Shipped names").
  ///
  /// The anchor and the steps must lead to a class or a metaclass; only
  /// `ClassMirror reflecting:`, which checks its argument, and navigation,
  /// which steps only to a class that exists, make them so. The way is
  /// read through the VM, by identity, and never sent a message, so a
  /// mirror made otherwise reads what the VM answers for whatever its
  /// anchor leads to: a `classFirst` that is not `true` takes no class, and
  /// a `steps` that is no count of steps walks to the end of the chain.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a class mirror that keeps the way to its class -- the
  /// anchor, whether the anchor's class comes first, and the steps -- as
  /// given, reading nothing yet; only its subclasses' factories send it.
  /// @param anObject the anchor; any object.
  /// @param aBoolean whether the way takes the anchor's class first; false
  /// when the anchor is the class itself.
  /// @param anInteger the number of superclass steps that follow, zero or
  /// more.
  private class AbstractClassMirror anchor: anObject classFirst: aBoolean steps: anInteger
      = Object (
    |
      /// The object the way to the class starts from; handed out only as
      /// the class a program gave `ClassMirror reflecting:`.
      private anchor = anObject.
      /// Whether the way takes the anchor's class first.
      /// Only its identity with `true` is asked of the VM; it is sent
      /// nothing, and anything else takes no class.
      private classFirst = aBoolean.
      /// The number of superclass steps after that.
      /// Compared by identity with each count of steps the walk has taken,
      /// through the VM; it is sent nothing.
      private steps = anInteger.
    |
  ) (
    /// Identifies the receiver as a class mirror, without a class test.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfClassMirror = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Hands out the class the mirror reflects, unless the mirror was
    /// reached by navigation and the class is a core-library one, whose
    /// structure stays readable. The class `ClassMirror reflecting:` was
    /// given is handed back whatever it is.
    ///
    /// @answers the class the mirror reflects.
    /// @signals Error 'reflectee: a core-library class reached by
    /// navigation is not handed out', when the mirror was reached by
    /// navigation and the class's mixin is a core-library one.
    public reflectee = (
      |
        held = self reflectedClass.
      |
      self isNavigated ifFalse: [^held].
      (vmMirror reflectionMixinIsShipped: (vmMirror reflectionMixinOf: held ifFail: [nil]) ifFail: [
        true.
      ]) ifTrue: [
        ^Error signal: 'reflectee: a core-library class reached by navigation is not handed out'.
      ].
      ^held.
    )

    /// Follows the way afresh through the VM: the anchor's class first when
    /// the way takes it, then as many superclasses as the steps count.
    ///
    /// Private, so that no subclass a program declares reads it.
    ///
    /// @answers the class the anchor and the steps lead to; nil past `Top`.
    private reflectedClass = (
      ^self walk: [:level :taken | level].
    )

    /// Walks the way and hands where it ends to `action`.
    ///
    /// Asks the VM whether the way takes the anchor's class and whether it
    /// has taken its steps, by identity, so that it sends `classFirst` and
    /// `steps` nothing.
    ///
    /// @param action a two-argument block, given the class the way leads
    /// to, nil past `Top`, and the number of superclass steps it took.
    /// @answers what `action` answers for where the way ends.
    private walk: action = (
      |
        level ::= self takesClassFirst ifTrue: [
          vmMirror objectClass: anchor ifFail: [nil].
        ] ifFalse: [
          anchor.
        ].
        taken ::= 0.
      |
      [
        (vmMirror reflectionObject: taken identicalTo: steps ifFail: [false]) or: [nil == level].
      ] whileFalse: [
        level:: vmMirror behaviorSuperclass: level ifFail: [nil].
        taken:: taken + 1.
      ].
      ^action value: level value: taken.
    )

    /// Tests the way's first step: whether `classFirst` is `true` itself,
    /// asked of the VM by identity.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the way takes the anchor's class first, a Boolean.
    private takesClassFirst = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionObject: classFirst identicalTo: true ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Tells whether the way takes any step from the anchor -- the
    /// anchor's class or a superclass -- which only navigation makes it
    /// take.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the mirror was reached by navigation, a Boolean.
    private isNavigated = (
      self takesClassFirst ifTrue: [^true].
      ^(vmMirror reflectionObject: steps identicalTo: 0 ifFail: [false]) not.
    )

    /// Compares the reflected class with `anObject` by identity; it sends
    /// `anObject` nothing.
    ///
    /// The comparison `=` makes of two class mirrors, which reads the
    /// class without handing it out: a mirror reached by navigation keeps
    /// its class back (the module's shipped-level rule).
    ///
    /// @param anObject any object.
    /// @answers whether the receiver reflects `anObject`, a Boolean.
    public reflects: anObject = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionObject: self reflectedClass identicalTo: anObject ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Reads the class's name: the name its declaration gives it, a
    /// metaclass's its class's name followed by ' class'. A level a `<:`
    /// clause adds is named for the class the clause names.
    ///
    /// The class's own name, as `Class>>name` answers it, rather than its
    /// mixin's: a declaration without a body is the level its last clause
    /// adds, whose mixin is the one that clause applies and is named for
    /// that mixin's declaration, while the class is the declaration's.
    ///
    /// @answers the class's name, a new String.
    public name = (
      |
        class = self reflectedClass.
      |
      self isMeta ifTrue: [
        ^(vmMirror className: (vmMirror metaclassThisClass: class ifFail: [nil]) ifFail: [nil])
            , ' class'.
      ].
      ^vmMirror className: class ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Reads the class's name as `name` does: a class's name is its
    /// declaration's, never qualified by the classes it is nested in.
    ///
    /// @answers the class's name, a new String.
    /// @see `name`.
    public simpleName = (
      ^self name.
    )

    /// Reflects the mixin the class applies: a class's instance side, a
    /// metaclass's class side.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on the class's mixin.
    public mixin = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinOf: self reflectedClass ifFail: [nil]).
    )

    /// Reflects the class's superclass through a mirror reached by
    /// navigation, one step further along the receiver's way, so its
    /// `reflectee` hands out the superclass only when it is the program's
    /// own (the module's shipped-level rule).
    ///
    /// @answers a new class mirror on the class's superclass, or nil for
    /// `Top`, which has none.
    public superclass = (
      ^self walk: [:level :taken |
        nil == (vmMirror behaviorSuperclass: level ifFail: [nil]) ifTrue: [
          nil.
        ] ifFalse: [
          NavigatedClassMirror anchor: anchor classFirst: self takesClassFirst steps: taken + 1.
        ].
      ].
    )

    /// Reflects the class's enclosing object: the object whose class
    /// declares it, nil for a module's class.
    ///
    /// @answers a new object mirror on the class's enclosing object.
    /// @signals Error 'enclosingObject: the enclosing object of a
    /// core-library class is not reflected', for a class whose mixin is a
    /// core-library one (the module's shipped-level rule).
    public enclosingObject = (
      ^ObjectMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionEnclosingObjectOf: self reflectedClass ifFail: [
        ^Error signal: 'enclosingObject: the enclosing object of a core-library class is not reflected'.
      ]).
    )

    /// Tells a metaclass from a class, read through the VM.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the class is a metaclass, a Boolean.
    public isMeta = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionIsMetaclass: self reflectedClass ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Lists the slot declarations of every level of the class, lazy ones
    /// left out: superclass level first, each level's in declaration
    /// order. A core-library level's are listed too: a declaration is
    /// structure, not a value.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of slot declaration mirrors on them.
    public slots = (
      ^self gathered: [:mixinMirror | mixinMirror slots].
    )

    /// Lists the methods every level of the class declares: superclass
    /// level first, each level's by their position in the source, then by
    /// selector. A method a subclass overrides is listed at both levels.
    /// Slot accessors, the factory and nested classes' accessors are not
    /// methods a declaration writes, so none is listed.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of method mirrors on them.
    public methods = (
      ^self gathered: [:mixinMirror | mixinMirror methods].
    )

    /// Lists the classes every level of the class declares nested in it:
    /// superclass level first, each level's in declaration order.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of class declaration mirrors on them.
    public nestedClasses = (
      ^self gathered: [:mixinMirror | mixinMirror nestedClasses].
    )

    /// Gathers the mirrors `members` answers for each level of the class,
    /// from `Top` down to the class itself, in that order.
    ///
    /// @param members a one-argument block, given a mixin mirror on one
    /// level's mixin and answering a MirrorGroup of that mixin's own
    /// members.
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of those mirrors, in that order.
    private gathered: members = (
      |
        levels ::= {}.
        level ::= self reflectedClass.
        result ::= {}.
      |
      [nil == level] whileFalse: [
        levels:: {level} , levels.
        level:: vmMirror behaviorSuperclass: level ifFail: [nil].
      ].
      levels do: [:each |
        |
          mixinMirror = MixinMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinOf: each ifFail: [nil]).
        |
        result:: result , (members value: mixinMirror) asArray.
      ].
      ^MirrorGroup over: result.
    )

    /// Compares the receiver with `other` by the identity of their classes,
    /// however each was reached; two applications of one mixin are two
    /// classes.
    ///
    /// Asymmetric for a program's subclass of `ClassMirror` against a
    /// mirror reached by navigation: the subclass's mirror trusts the
    /// module's `NavigatedClassMirror` and answers true for one on its
    /// class, but the navigated mirror trusts only the module's own mirror
    /// classes and answers false, so that a class it holds back never
    /// reaches program code through `reflects:`.
    ///
    /// @param other any object; sent `reflects:` only when `trusts:` trusts
    /// its class, so that the class is handed to no other code.
    /// @answers whether `other` is a class mirror on the same class.
    public = other = (
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: self identicalTo: other ifFail: [false]) ifTrue: [^true].
      (self trusts: (vmMirror objectClass: other ifFail: [nil])) ifFalse: [^false].
      ^other reflects: self reflectedClass.
    )

    /// Decides whether `=` may hand the reflected class to instances of
    /// `aClass`: this module's `ClassMirror` or `NavigatedClassMirror`,
    /// whose code is this module's, or, for a mirror not reached by
    /// navigation, the receiver's own class, whose instances a program made
    /// over a class it holds. A mirror reached by navigation trusts no
    /// class a program declared, whose `reflects:` could keep a class the
    /// program was never given.
    ///
    /// @param aClass the class of the object `=` compares the receiver
    /// with.
    /// @answers whether `aClass` is a class whose instances `=` may hand
    /// the reflected class to, a Boolean.
    private trusts: aClass = (
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: aClass identicalTo: outer MirrorsFactory ClassMirror ifFail: [
        false.
      ]) ifTrue: [^true].
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: aClass
          identicalTo: outer MirrorsFactory NavigatedClassMirror
          ifFail: [false]) ifTrue: [^true].
      self isNavigated ifTrue: [^false].
      ^vmMirror reflectionObject: aClass
          identicalTo: (vmMirror objectClass: self ifFail: [nil])
          ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Hashes the receiver by its class's identity, so that two mirrors on
    /// the one class hash alike.
    ///
    /// @answers the class's identity hash.
    public hash = (
      ^vmMirror objectHash: self reflectedClass ifFail: [0].
    )
  )

  /// A mirror on one class or metaclass a program gives it: it reads the
  /// class as every class mirror does (`AbstractClassMirror`), and its
  /// `reflectee` hands the class back, whatever it is.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror whose way is `aClass` itself -- no class
  /// first, no step -- and asks the VM, sending `aClass` nothing, whether
  /// it is a class or a metaclass.
  /// @param aClass a class or a metaclass.
  /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `aClass`, 'reflecting: requires a
  /// class or a metaclass', for anything else.
  private class ClassMirror reflecting: aClass
      = AbstractClassMirror anchor: aClass classFirst: false steps: 0 (
    vmMirror reflectionIsMetaclass: aClass ifFail: [
      (ArgumentError value: aClass) signal: 'reflecting: requires a class or a metaclass'.
    ].
  ) ()

  /// A class mirror a program reached by navigation -- an object's class,
  /// a superclass -- rather than made itself: it reads the class as a
  /// `ClassMirror` does, but hands the class out only when its mixin is
  /// not a core-library one (the module's shipped-level rule). Every
  /// navigation answers one of these, never a `ClassMirror`.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror over the way from `anObject`, kept as
  /// `AbstractClassMirror`'s factory keeps it; only an object mirror's
  /// `getClass` and a class mirror's `superclass` send it.
  /// @param anObject the anchor, as for `AbstractClassMirror`: the object an
  /// object mirror reflects, or the class a class mirror was given.
  /// @param aBoolean whether the way takes the anchor's class first.
  /// @param anInteger the number of superclass steps that follow.
  private class NavigatedClassMirror anchor: anObject classFirst: aBoolean steps: anInteger
      = AbstractClassMirror anchor: anObject classFirst: aBoolean steps: anInteger () ()

  /// One slot of an object an object mirror reflects: its name and, as an
  /// object mirror, its value, read when the object's `slots` were.
  ///
  /// @factory makes the mirror on the slot named `aSymbol` that held
  /// `anObject`, wrapping the value in a new object mirror at once.
  /// @param aSymbol the slot's name.
  /// @param anObject the slot's value.
  private class SlotMirror name: aSymbol value: anObject = Object (
    |
      /// The slot's name, a Symbol.
      /// One of the names the VM listed for the object when its `slots`
      /// were read.
      public name = aSymbol.
      /// An object mirror on the slot's value.
      /// Made when the object's `slots` were read, so it reflects the
      /// value the slot held then, whatever the slot holds later.
      public value = ObjectMirror reflecting: anObject.
    |
  ) ()

  /// A fixed sequence of mirrors, in the order the mirror that answered
  /// it gives: slots in declaration order, superclass first; methods by
  /// their position in the source, then by selector; nested classes in
  /// declaration order. It never changes.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a group over `anArray`, which it keeps rather than
  /// copies.
  /// @param anArray an Array of mirrors, each answering `name`; kept, not
  /// copied, so whoever builds the group hands it over.
  private class MirrorGroup over: anArray = Object (
    |
      /// The mirrors, in the group's order.
      /// Never changed after the factory; `asArray` answers a copy of it.
      private mirrors = anArray.
    |
  ) (
    /// Counts the mirrors.
    ///
    /// @answers the number of mirrors, an Integer.
    public size = (
      ^mirrors size.
    )

    /// Tests the group for mirrors.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the group holds no mirror, a Boolean.
    public isEmpty = (
      ^mirrors isEmpty.
    )

    /// Evaluates `action` with each mirror in turn, in the group's order.
    ///
    /// @param action a one-argument block.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 1', for an `action` that does not
    /// take one argument, when the group is not empty.
    public do: action = (
      mirrors do: action.
    )

    /// Evaluates `transform` with each mirror in turn, in the group's
    /// order, and collects what it answers.
    ///
    /// @param transform a one-argument block.
    /// @answers a new Array of what `transform` answers for each mirror,
    /// in the group's order.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 1', for a `transform` that does not
    /// take one argument, when the group is not empty.
    public collect: transform = (
      ^mirrors collect: transform.
    )

    /// Finds the first mirror, in the group's order, for which `predicate`
    /// answers true.
    ///
    /// @param predicate a one-argument block answering a Boolean.
    /// @param onNone a block of no arguments.
    /// @answers that mirror, or what `onNone` answers when there is none.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 1', for a `predicate` that does not
    /// take one argument, when the group is not empty.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for an `onNone` that declares any
    /// parameter, when no mirror matches.
    public detect: predicate ifNone: onNone = (
      ^mirrors detect: predicate ifNone: onNone.
    )

    /// Finds the first mirror, in the group's order, whose name has the
    /// text of `aName`.
    ///
    /// @param aName a String or a Symbol; a Symbol and a String of one
    /// text name the same mirror.
    /// @answers that mirror, or nil when there is none.
    public findMirrorNamed: aName = (
      |
        text = aName asString.
      |
      ^mirrors detect: [:each | each name asString = text] ifNone: [nil].
    )

    /// Tests whether a mirror of the group has the name `aName`, as
    /// `findMirrorNamed:` compares it.
    ///
    /// @param aName a String or a Symbol.
    /// @answers whether the group has such a mirror, a Boolean.
    /// @see `findMirrorNamed:`.
    public includesMirrorNamed: aName = (
      ^(self findMirrorNamed: aName) isNil not.
    )

    /// Copies the mirrors out, in the group's order, so changing the copy
    /// leaves the group as it was.
    ///
    /// @answers a new Array of the mirrors.
    public asArray = (
      ^Array withAll: mirrors.
    )
  )

  /// A mirror on one mixin -- a class declaration's instance side or its
  /// class side, declared or synthesized -- and the members its own
  /// declaration declares, never inherited ones. Everything is read
  /// through the VM. A mixin is one however many classes apply it, so two
  /// mirrors on it are equal however each was reached.
  ///
  /// What stays readable of a core-library mixin is its structure, which
  /// is all a mixin mirror answers (the module's shipped-level rule).
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror on `aReifiedMixin`, which it keeps and never
  /// hands out.
  /// @param aReifiedMixin the kernel's reified mixin, as the VM answers it
  /// for a class's mixin; one object per mixin.
  private class MixinMirror reflecting: aReifiedMixin = Object (
    |
      /// The reified mixin the mirror reflects; never handed out.
      /// Given only to the VM, to this module's mirrors and to the
      /// `reflects:` of a mirror `trusts:` trusts.
      private subject = aReifiedMixin.
    |
  ) (
    /// Identifies the receiver as a mixin mirror, without a class test.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfMixinMirror = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Compares the reflected mixin with `anObject` by identity; it sends
    /// `anObject` nothing.
    ///
    /// The comparison `=` makes of two mixin mirrors, which reads the
    /// reified mixin without handing it out.
    ///
    /// @param anObject any object.
    /// @answers whether the receiver reflects `anObject`, a Boolean.
    public reflects: anObject = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionObject: subject identicalTo: anObject ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Reads the mixin's name: its declaration's, a class side's that name
    /// followed by ' class'.
    ///
    /// @answers the mixin's name, a new String.
    public name = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionMixinName: subject ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Reads the mixin's name as `name` does: a mixin's name is its
    /// declaration's, never qualified by the classes it is nested in.
    ///
    /// @answers the mixin's name, a new String.
    /// @see `name`.
    public simpleName = (
      ^self name.
    )

    /// Tells a class side from an instance side, read through the VM.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the mixin is a class side, a Boolean.
    public isMeta = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionMixinIsMeta: subject ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Reflects the instance side of the class declaration the mixin's
    /// class declaration is nested in. A class side is enclosed by what
    /// its instance side is.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on that instance side, or nil for a
    /// module's class.
    public enclosingMixin = (
      |
        enclosing = vmMirror reflectionMixinEnclosing: subject ifFail: [nil].
      |
      nil == enclosing ifTrue: [^nil].
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: enclosing.
    )

    /// Reflects the class side of the mixin's declaration -- the one it
    /// declares, or the one synthesized for a declaration that declares
    /// none.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on that class side, on the receiver's
    /// mixin itself for a class side.
    public classMixin = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinClassSide: subject ifFail: [nil]).
    )

    /// Reflects the instance side of the mixin's declaration.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on that instance side, on the
    /// receiver's mixin itself for an instance side.
    public instanceMixin = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinInstanceSide: subject ifFail: [nil]).
    )

    /// Reflects the declaration the mixin is a side of: the same for an
    /// instance side and its class side.
    ///
    /// @answers a new class declaration mirror on that declaration.
    public declaration = (
      ^ClassDeclarationMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinInstanceSide: subject ifFail: [
        nil.
      ]).
    )

    /// Lists the mixin's own eager slot declarations, in declaration
    /// order.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of slot declaration mirrors on them;
    /// empty for a class side.
    public slots = (
      ^self slotsLazy: false.
    )

    /// Lists the mixin's own lazy slot declarations, in declaration
    /// order.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of slot declaration mirrors on them;
    /// empty for a class side.
    public lazySlots = (
      ^self slotsLazy: true.
    )

    /// Lists those of the mixin's own slot declarations that are lazy, or
    /// eager, as asked, in declaration order.
    ///
    /// @param lazy true for the lazy declarations, false for the eager
    /// ones.
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of slot declaration mirrors on them.
    private slotsLazy: lazy = (
      |
        declarations = vmMirror reflectionMixinSlots: subject ifFail: [{}].
        result ::= {}.
      |
      declarations do: [:entry |
        (entry at: 4) == lazy ifTrue: [
          result:: result
              , {
                SlotDeclarationMirror in: subject
                    name: (entry at: 1)
                    mutable: (entry at: 2)
                    access: (entry at: 3)
                    lazy: (entry at: 4).
              }.
        ].
      ].
      ^MirrorGroup over: result.
    )

    /// Lists the methods the mixin's declaration writes, by their position
    /// in the source, then by selector. Slot accessors, a lazy slot's
    /// getter, the factory and nested classes' accessors are not methods a
    /// declaration writes, so none is listed.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of method mirrors on them.
    public methods = (
      |
        entries = vmMirror reflectionMixinMethods: subject ifFail: [{}].
      |
      ^MirrorGroup over: (entries collect: [:entry |
        MethodMirror in: subject selector: (entry at: 1) access: (entry at: 2).
      ]).
    )

    /// Lists the classes the mixin declares nested in it, in declaration
    /// order.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of class declaration mirrors on them;
    /// empty for a class side.
    public nestedClasses = (
      |
        nested = vmMirror reflectionMixinNested: subject ifFail: [{}].
      |
      ^MirrorGroup over: (nested collect: [:each | ClassDeclarationMirror reflecting: each]).
    )

    /// Compares the receiver with `other` by the identity of the one
    /// object that stands for the mixin, however each mirror was reached;
    /// the mixin of two applications is one mixin.
    ///
    /// @param other any object; sent `reflects:` only when it is an
    /// instance of this module's `MixinMirror` or of the receiver's class,
    /// so that the reified mixin is handed to no other code.
    /// @answers whether `other` is a mixin mirror on the same mixin, a
    /// Boolean.
    public = other = (
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: self identicalTo: other ifFail: [false]) ifTrue: [^true].
      (self trusts: (vmMirror objectClass: other ifFail: [nil])) ifFalse: [^false].
      ^other reflects: subject.
    )

    /// Decides whether `=` may hand the reified mixin to instances of
    /// `aClass`: this module's `MixinMirror`, whose code is this module's,
    /// or the receiver's own class.
    ///
    /// @param aClass the class of the object `=` compares the receiver
    /// with.
    /// @answers whether `aClass` is a class whose instances `=` may hand
    /// the reified mixin to, a Boolean.
    private trusts: aClass = (
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: aClass identicalTo: outer MirrorsFactory MixinMirror ifFail: [
        false.
      ]) ifTrue: [^true].
      ^vmMirror reflectionObject: aClass
          identicalTo: (vmMirror objectClass: self ifFail: [nil])
          ifFail: [false].
    )

    /// Hashes the receiver by the reified mixin's identity, so that two
    /// mirrors on the one mixin hash alike.
    ///
    /// @answers the reified mixin's identity hash.
    public hash = (
      ^vmMirror objectHash: subject ifFail: [0].
    )
  )

  /// A mirror on one class declaration: its name, its two sides, the
  /// declaration it is nested in, its access and its text. It is named by
  /// the reified mixin of its instance side, so the declarations reached
  /// from either side, or from the enclosing declaration's nested
  /// classes, are equal.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror on the declaration whose instance side is
  /// `aReifiedMixin`, which it keeps and never hands out.
  /// @param aReifiedMixin the reified mixin of the declaration's instance
  /// side.
  private class ClassDeclarationMirror reflecting: aReifiedMixin = Object (
    |
      /// The reified mixin of the declaration's instance side; never
      /// handed out.
      private subject = aReifiedMixin.
    |
  ) (
    /// Identifies the receiver as a class declaration mirror, without a
    /// class test; `=` sends it to the object it compares the receiver
    /// with.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfClassDeclarationMirror = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Reads the name the declaration gives the class.
    ///
    /// @answers that name, a new String.
    public name = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionMixinName: subject ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Reflects the declaration's instance side.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on the declaration's instance side.
    public instanceSide = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: subject.
    )

    /// Reflects the declaration's class side, the synthesized one of a
    /// declaration that declares none.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on the declaration's class side.
    public classSide = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinClassSide: subject ifFail: [nil]).
    )

    /// Reflects the declaration this one is nested in.
    ///
    /// @answers a new class declaration mirror on that declaration, or nil
    /// for a module's class.
    public enclosingClass = (
      |
        enclosing = self instanceSide enclosingMixin.
      |
      nil == enclosing ifTrue: [^nil].
      ^enclosing declaration.
    )

    /// Reads the access of the class's accessor; an unmarked declaration's
    /// is `#protected`.
    ///
    /// @answers the Symbol `#public`, `#protected` or `#private`.
    public accessModifier = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionMixinAccess: subject ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Reads the declaration's text, from its access modifier, or `class`
    /// when it has none, to its closing parenthesis, as its source spells
    /// it. An image may carry no source.
    ///
    /// @answers that text, a new String; nil when the code was built
    /// without its source.
    public source = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionMixinSource: subject ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Opens a builder over the declaration, which stages edits of its
    /// header, its methods and its lazy slots apart from the live class
    /// until its `install`. A class an image decoded is edited from the
    /// text the image carries.
    ///
    /// @answers a new ClassDeclarationBuilder over the declaration.
    /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic, and answers no builder,
    /// when the declaration may not be edited: '<name> belongs to the
    /// shipped core library, which no MirrorBuilder edits' for a class of a
    /// shipped core-library module, this one and the kernel among them;
    /// and '<name> has no source text to edit' for one built without its
    /// module's text.
    public asBuilder = (
      ^ClassDeclarationBuilder reflecting: subject.
    )

    /// Compares the receiver with `other` by their instance sides: a
    /// declaration is never equal to either of its sides.
    ///
    /// @param other any object; sent `isKindOfClassDeclarationMirror`, and
    /// `instanceSide` when it answers true.
    /// @answers whether `other` is a class declaration mirror on the same
    /// declaration: one whose instance side is the receiver's; a Boolean.
    public = other = (
      other isKindOfClassDeclarationMirror ifFalse: [^false].
      ^self instanceSide = other instanceSide.
    )

    /// Hashes the receiver as its instance side's mirror hashes, so that
    /// two mirrors on the one declaration hash alike.
    ///
    /// @answers the hash of the declaration's instance side.
    public hash = (
      ^self instanceSide hash.
    )
  )

  /// A mirror on one method a mixin's declaration writes: its selector,
  /// its access, the mixin and the method's text. Two mirrors on one
  /// selector of one mixin are equal, however each was reached.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror on the method `aSymbol` of `aReifiedMixin`,
  /// keeping the three arguments as given; a mixin mirror's `methods`
  /// sends it.
  /// @param aReifiedMixin the reified mixin that declares the method.
  /// @param aSymbol the method's selector.
  /// @param anAccessSymbol the method's access, `#public`, `#protected` or
  /// `#private`.
  private class MethodMirror in: aReifiedMixin selector: aSymbol access: anAccessSymbol = Object (
    |
      /// The reified mixin that declares the method; never handed out.
      /// Given only to the VM and to the mixin mirror `definingMixin`
      /// makes.
      private mixin = aReifiedMixin.
      /// The method's selector, a Symbol.
      /// `name` answers it, and `source` looks the method up by it.
      private selector = aSymbol.
      /// The method's access, `#public`, `#protected` or `#private`.
      /// As the VM listed it beside the selector; `accessModifier`
      /// answers it.
      private access = anAccessSymbol.
    |
  ) (
    /// Identifies the receiver as a method mirror, without a class test;
    /// `=` sends it to the object it compares the receiver with.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfMethodMirror = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Reads the method's selector.
    ///
    /// @answers the method's selector, a Symbol.
    public name = (
      ^selector.
    )

    /// Reads the method's access; an unmarked method's is `#protected`.
    ///
    /// @answers the Symbol `#public`, `#protected` or `#private`.
    public accessModifier = (
      ^access.
    )

    /// Reflects the mixin whose declaration writes the method.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on that mixin.
    public definingMixin = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: mixin.
    )

    /// Reads the method's text, from its access modifier to its closing
    /// parenthesis, as its source spells it, the comments before it left
    /// out. An image may carry no source.
    ///
    /// @answers that text, a new String; nil when the code was built
    /// without its source.
    public source = (
      ^vmMirror reflectionMixin: mixin methodSource: selector ifFail: [nil].
    )

    /// Compares the receiver with `other` by the identity of their
    /// selectors and by their defining mixins.
    ///
    /// @param other any object; sent `isKindOfMethodMirror`, and `name` and
    /// `definingMixin` when it answers true.
    /// @answers whether `other` is a method mirror on the same selector of
    /// the same mixin, a Boolean.
    public = other = (
      other isKindOfMethodMirror ifFalse: [^false].
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: selector identicalTo: other name ifFail: [false]) ifFalse: [
        ^false.
      ].
      ^self definingMixin = other definingMixin.
    )

    /// Combines the identity hashes of the mixin and the selector, so that
    /// two mirrors on the one method hash alike.
    ///
    /// @answers a hash of the mixin and the selector.
    public hash = (
      ^(vmMirror objectHash: mixin ifFail: [0]) bitXor: (vmMirror objectHash: selector ifFail: [0]).
    )
  )

  /// A mirror on one slot a mixin's declaration declares: its name, its
  /// mutability, whether it is lazy, its access and the mixin. Two mirrors
  /// on one name of one mixin are equal, however each was reached.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a mirror on the slot declaration `aSymbol` of
  /// `aReifiedMixin`, keeping the five arguments as given; a mixin mirror's
  /// `slots` and `lazySlots` send it.
  /// @param aReifiedMixin the reified mixin that declares the slot.
  /// @param aSymbol the slot's name.
  /// @param aBoolean whether the slot is mutable.
  /// @param anAccessSymbol the slot's access, `#public`, `#protected` or
  /// `#private`.
  /// @param isLazy whether the slot is lazy.
  private class SlotDeclarationMirror
      in: aReifiedMixin
      name: aSymbol
      mutable: aBoolean
      access: anAccessSymbol
      lazy: isLazy
      = Object (
    |
      /// The reified mixin that declares the slot; never handed out.
      /// Given only to the VM and to the mixin mirror `definingMixin`
      /// makes.
      private mixin = aReifiedMixin.
      /// The slot's name, a Symbol.
      /// As the VM listed it for the mixin; `name` answers it.
      private slotName = aSymbol.
      /// Whether the slot is mutable.
      /// True for a slot declared with `::=`, as the VM listed it;
      /// `isMutable` answers it.
      private mutable = aBoolean.
      /// The slot's access, `#public`, `#protected` or `#private`.
      /// As the VM listed it beside the name; `accessModifier` answers it.
      private access = anAccessSymbol.
      /// Whether the slot is lazy.
      /// The very `true` or `false` the mixin mirror asked for, since it
      /// keeps only the declarations whose flag is that object.
      private lazySlot = isLazy.
    |
  ) (
    /// Identifies the receiver as a slot declaration mirror, without a
    /// class test; `=` sends it to the object it compares the receiver
    /// with.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfSlotDeclarationMirror = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Reads the slot's name.
    ///
    /// @answers the slot's name, a Symbol.
    public name = (
      ^slotName.
    )

    /// Tells a slot declared with `::=` from one declared with `=`.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the slot is mutable, a Boolean.
    public isMutable = (
      ^mutable.
    )

    /// Tells a lazy slot from an eager one.
    ///
    /// @answers whether the slot is lazy, a Boolean.
    public isLazy = (
      ^lazySlot.
    )

    /// Reads the slot's access; an unmarked slot's is `#protected`.
    ///
    /// @answers the Symbol `#public`, `#protected` or `#private`.
    public accessModifier = (
      ^access.
    )

    /// Reflects the mixin whose declaration declares the slot.
    ///
    /// @answers a new mixin mirror on that mixin.
    public definingMixin = (
      ^MixinMirror reflecting: mixin.
    )

    /// Compares the receiver with `other` by the identity of their names
    /// and by their defining mixins, a mixin declaring a name once.
    ///
    /// @param other any object; sent `isKindOfSlotDeclarationMirror`, and
    /// `name` and `definingMixin` when it answers true.
    /// @answers whether `other` is a slot declaration mirror on the same
    /// name of the same mixin, a Boolean.
    public = other = (
      other isKindOfSlotDeclarationMirror ifFalse: [^false].
      (vmMirror reflectionObject: slotName identicalTo: other name ifFail: [false]) ifFalse: [
        ^false.
      ].
      ^self definingMixin = other definingMixin.
    )

    /// Combines the identity hashes of the mixin and the name, so that two
    /// mirrors on the one slot declaration hash alike.
    ///
    /// @answers a hash of the mixin and the name.
    public hash = (
      ^(vmMirror objectHash: mixin ifFail: [0]) bitXor: (vmMirror objectHash: slotName ifFail: [0]).
    )
  )

  /// A builder over one class declaration of a program, the MirrorBuilder
  /// `ClassDeclarationMirror>>asBuilder` answers: it stages edits of the
  /// declaration's header, of its instance side's methods and lazy slots
  /// and of its class side's methods, and `install` makes them visible at
  /// once to every class that applies the declaration's mixin, migrating
  /// the instances whose slots changed, or changes nothing. Until then
  /// nothing a program observes changes.
  ///
  /// Every edit is checked as it is staged: the VM splices it, with every
  /// edit staged before it, into the module's current text, then parses
  /// and resolves the module, and an edit it refuses -- a syntax error, a
  /// member that collides with another, a header that renames the class
  /// or changes its access or its superclass -- signals an Error with the diagnostic and
  /// leaves the builder as it was, so a later `install` installs only the
  /// edits that were accepted.
  ///
  /// The staged state is Strings and Symbols, never a compiled member, so
  /// nothing exists outside the object space before `install`. Each check
  /// and the install start from the module's current text, so an install
  /// another builder made meanwhile is under this one's: two edits that
  /// each pass their own check can still fail together at the second
  /// install.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a builder over the declaration whose instance side is
  /// `aReifiedMixin`, with nothing staged, and checks that empty edit at
  /// once, which reads the declaration's text, as `source` answers it,
  /// and its header, as `header source` answers it.
  /// @param aReifiedMixin the reified mixin of the declaration's instance
  /// side.
  /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic when the declaration may not
  /// be edited at all (`ClassDeclarationMirror>>asBuilder` lists them).
  /// @see `ClassDeclarationMirror>>asBuilder`.
  private class ClassDeclarationBuilder reflecting: aReifiedMixin = Object (
    |
      /// The reified mixin of the declaration's instance side; never
      /// handed out.
      private subject = aReifiedMixin.
      /// The staged header's text, a String, or nil to keep the
      /// declaration's.
      private headerText ::= nil.
      /// The staged operations on the instance side, in the order they
      /// were staged: an Array of two-element Arrays, an operation's
      /// Symbol and its text or name, as the VM reads an edit.
      private instanceOperations ::= {}.
      /// The staged operations on the class side, method operations only,
      /// as `instanceOperations` holds them.
      private classOperations ::= {}.
      /// The staged declaration's text, a String, as the last check or
      /// install answered it.
      private stagedSource ::= nil.
      /// The staged declaration's header, a String, as the last check or
      /// install answered it: the parse's, up to the members'
      /// parenthesis.
      private stagedHeader ::= nil.
      /// The declaration's header, a ClassHeaderBuilder, which stages a
      /// new header through the receiver.
      public header = ClassHeaderBuilder reading: [
        stagedHeader.
      ] staging: [:text |
        self stageHeader: text.
      ].
      /// The declaration's instance side, a MixinBuilder whose methods and
      /// lazy slots stage through the receiver.
      public instanceSide = MixinBuilder methods: (MutableMemberGroup adding: #addMethod
          removing: #removeMethod
          staging: [:operation | self stage: operation onClassSide: false])
          lazySlots: (MutableMemberGroup adding: #addLazySlot
              removing: #removeLazySlot
              staging: [:operation | self stage: operation onClassSide: false])
          mixin: (MixinMirror reflecting: aReifiedMixin).
      /// The declaration's class side, a MixinBuilder whose methods stage
      /// through the receiver; it has no lazy slots.
      public classSide = MixinBuilder methods: (MutableMemberGroup adding: #addMethod
          removing: #removeMethod
          staging: [:operation | self stage: operation onClassSide: true])
          lazySlots: nil
          mixin: (MixinMirror reflecting: (vmMirror reflectionMixinClassSide: aReifiedMixin
              ifFail: [nil])).
    |
    self check: {nil. {}. {}}.
  ) (
    /// Shows the declaration as the staged edits make it: its text, from
    /// its access modifier, or `class` when it has none, to its closing
    /// parenthesis, with every edit staged since the builder was made or
    /// last installed spliced in, as the last check answered it. With
    /// nothing staged it is the text the declaration mirror's `source`
    /// answers. A staged header starts it; a staged method or lazy slot
    /// that replaces a member stands where the member stood, and one that
    /// adds a member stands last on its side.
    ///
    /// @answers the staged declaration's text, a String.
    public source = (
      ^stagedSource.
    )

    /// Installs every staged edit at once: every class that applies the
    /// declaration's mixin answers the new methods from the next send on,
    /// and every instance whose class's slots changed is replaced, keeping
    /// its identity, by one of the new layout whose slots of an old name
    /// keep their values and whose new slots are nil, their initializers
    /// not run. A method or a closure already running finishes with the
    /// code it was running.
    ///
    /// @answers the receiver, which then stands for the installed
    /// declaration, with nothing staged.
    /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic, changing nothing -- neither
    /// the class, nor its instances, nor what the receiver stages -- when
    /// the staged edits no longer apply to the module's current text, as
    /// when another builder's install gave the class a slot of the name of
    /// a staged method; and 'cannot migrate an instance of <class name>,
    /// which is not an ordinary object' when an instance whose layout would
    /// change cannot be copied into the new one.
    public install = (
      |
        answer = vmMirror reflectionMixin: subject installEdit: self edit ifFail: [
          ^self refuseEdit.
        ].
      |
      (answer at: 1) ifFalse: [^Error signal: (answer at: 2)].
      headerText:: nil.
      instanceOperations:: {}.
      classOperations:: {}.
      stagedSource:: answer at: 2.
      stagedHeader:: answer at: 3.
    )

    /// Assembles the staged edit in the form the VM reads.
    ///
    /// @answers a new Array of the header's text or nil, the instance
    /// side's operations and the class side's.
    private edit = (
      ^{headerText. instanceOperations. classOperations}.
    )

    /// Stages `operation` on one side, after every operation staged
    /// there before it, when the check accepts the result.
    ///
    /// @param operation a two-element Array, an operation's Symbol and its
    /// text or name.
    /// @param classSide true for the class side, false for the instance
    /// side.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals Error the one `check:` signals, staging nothing.
    /// @see `check:`.
    private stage: operation onClassSide: classSide = (
      classSide ifTrue: [
        self check: {headerText. instanceOperations. classOperations , {operation}}.
      ] ifFalse: [
        self check: {headerText. instanceOperations , {operation}. classOperations}.
      ].
    )

    /// Stages `text` as the declaration's header, in place of any header
    /// staged before, when the check accepts the result.
    ///
    /// @param text a String, the header as `ClassHeaderBuilder>>source:`
    /// takes it.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals Error the one `check:` signals, staging nothing.
    /// @see `check:`.
    private stageHeader: text = (
      self check: {text. instanceOperations. classOperations}.
    )

    /// Checks `newState` against the module's current text and, when the
    /// VM accepts it, makes it the staged state, the declaration's text
    /// and the header the check answers becoming `source` and the
    /// header's `source`. Nothing else changes either way.
    ///
    /// @param newState an Array of the header's text or nil, the instance
    /// side's operations and the class side's, as `edit` answers them.
    /// @answers the receiver, once the VM accepted `newState`.
    /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic, leaving the staged state as
    /// it was, when the check refuses the edit; and the one `refuseEdit`
    /// signals when the VM cannot read it.
    private check: newState = (
      |
        answer = vmMirror reflectionMixin: subject checkEdit: newState ifFail: [^self refuseEdit].
      |
      (answer at: 1) ifFalse: [^Error signal: (answer at: 2)].
      headerText:: newState at: 1.
      instanceOperations:: newState at: 2.
      classOperations:: newState at: 3.
      stagedSource:: answer at: 2.
      stagedHeader:: answer at: 3.
    )

    /// Refuses an edit the VM cannot read: one whose text, after
    /// `asString`, is no String, or whose name, after `asSymbol`, is no
    /// Symbol. It never returns: an Error is not resumable.
    ///
    /// @answers nothing; it never returns.
    /// @signals Error 'a MirrorBuilder takes a member or a header as a
    /// String and a name as a Symbol'.
    private refuseEdit = (
      ^Error signal: 'a MirrorBuilder takes a member or a header as a String and a name as a Symbol'.
    )
  )

  /// The header of a declaration a ClassDeclarationBuilder edits: its text
  /// -- the class's access modifier, name, factory, superclass clause,
  /// slots and initializer -- as the builder's last check or install
  /// answered it, and replaced through the builder.
  ///
  /// The header's extent is the parse's, which the VM answers with every
  /// check: reading it here would take a second reading of the syntax,
  /// which would have to follow every rule of the lexer to agree with it.
  ///
  /// @factory makes the header over the builder's two blocks, keeping them
  /// as given; a ClassDeclarationBuilder's `header` slot sends it.
  /// @param aReadBlock a block of no arguments that answers the builder's
  /// staged header, a String.
  /// @param aStageBlock a one-argument block that stages a header's text,
  /// a String, through the builder, signalling what the builder's check
  /// signals.
  private class ClassHeaderBuilder reading: aReadBlock staging: aStageBlock = Object (
    |
      /// The block that answers the builder's staged header.
      /// Evaluated afresh by every `source`, so it reads what the
      /// builder's last check or install answered.
      private reading = aReadBlock.
      /// The block that stages a new header through the builder.
      /// Evaluated by `source:` with the header's text, a String; it
      /// signals what the builder's check signals.
      private staging = aStageBlock.
    |
  ) (
    /// Reads the staged header's text: the staged declaration's text from
    /// its start up to, not including, the parenthesis that opens its
    /// members -- the text `source:` was last given, as it was given, or
    /// the declaration's own header when none is staged; all of the
    /// declaration's text for one with no members of its own.
    ///
    /// @answers the staged header's text, a String.
    public source = (
      ^reading value.
    )

    /// Stages `aString` as the declaration's header. The header replaces
    /// the declaration's text from its start up to its members'
    /// parenthesis, so it starts exactly where the declaration does --
    /// with its access modifier, or `class` when it has none, with no
    /// whitespace or comment before it -- and holds the class's name,
    /// factory, superclass clause, slots and initializer:
    /// `public class Foo = Bar (| x |)`.
    ///
    /// @param aString the header's text, a String or a Symbol, sent
    /// `asString`.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic, staging nothing, for a
    /// header that does not parse or does not end where the members begin,
    /// one that renames the class ('the header renames <name> to <new
    /// name>; an edit keeps a class's name'), one that changes its access
    /// ('the header changes the access of <name>; an edit keeps it'; no
    /// modifier and `protected` are one access), one that changes its
    /// superclass clause or its `<:` clauses ('the header changes the
    /// superclass of <name>; an edit keeps it'), and one whose slots
    /// collide with a member staged or declared. The superclass and `<:`
    /// clauses are compared as text, so a header that changes only the
    /// whitespace or comments inside them is refused as well.
    public source: aString = (
      staging value: aString asString.
    )
  )

  /// One side of a declaration a ClassDeclarationBuilder edits, the
  /// instance side or the class side: its methods and, on the instance
  /// side, its lazy slots, each a MutableMemberGroup that stages through
  /// the builder; and the live side's slots, which an edit changes only
  /// through the header.
  ///
  /// @factory makes one side of a builder's declaration over the groups
  /// and the mirror it is given, keeping them as given; a
  /// ClassDeclarationBuilder's `instanceSide` and `classSide` slots send
  /// it.
  /// @param aMethodGroup the MutableMemberGroup of the side's methods.
  /// @param aLazySlotGroup the MutableMemberGroup of the side's lazy
  /// slots, or nil for a class side, which declares none.
  /// @param aMixinMirror a mixin mirror on the side's live mixin.
  private class MixinBuilder methods: aMethodGroup lazySlots: aLazySlotGroup mixin: aMixinMirror
      = Object (
    |
      /// The group of the side's methods.
      /// `methods` answers it itself, so every edit through it stages
      /// through the builder.
      private methodGroup = aMethodGroup.
      /// The group of the side's lazy slots, nil for a class side.
      /// `lazySlots` answers it itself, and refuses the class side for
      /// its nil.
      private lazySlotGroup = aLazySlotGroup.
      /// A mixin mirror on the side's live mixin.
      /// Asked afresh by every `slots`, so what it lists is the live
      /// mixin's, never a staged header's.
      private mixin = aMixinMirror.
    |
  ) (
    /// Hands out the side's methods, which stage the addition,
    /// replacement and removal of a method through the builder.
    ///
    /// @answers the side's MutableMemberGroup of methods.
    public methods = (
      ^methodGroup.
    )

    /// Hands out the instance side's lazy slots, which stage the
    /// addition, replacement and removal of a lazy slot through the
    /// builder.
    ///
    /// @answers the instance side's MutableMemberGroup of lazy slots.
    /// @signals Error 'lazySlots: a class side declares no lazy slots', on
    /// the class side.
    public lazySlots = (
      nil == lazySlotGroup ifTrue: [
        ^Error signal: 'lazySlots: a class side declares no lazy slots'.
      ].
      ^lazySlotGroup.
    )

    /// Lists the live side's own eager slots, in declaration order, as
    /// `MixinMirror>>slots` answers them: what the last install made,
    /// never a staged header's.
    ///
    /// @answers a new MirrorGroup of slot declaration mirrors on them;
    /// empty for a class side.
    /// @see `MixinMirror>>slots`.
    public slots = (
      ^mixin slots.
    )
  )

  /// One group of a side's members a ClassDeclarationBuilder edits -- a
  /// side's methods, or the instance side's lazy slots: it stages, through
  /// the builder, the addition or replacement of a member from its text
  /// and the removal of one by its name. It answers no mirrors; the
  /// builder's `source` answers what is staged.
  ///
  /// @factory makes a group that stages its additions as `anAddSymbol`
  /// and its removals as `aRemoveSymbol` through `aBlock`, keeping the
  /// three as given.
  /// @param anAddSymbol the Symbol of the operation that adds or replaces
  /// a member, `#addMethod` or `#addLazySlot`.
  /// @param aRemoveSymbol the Symbol of the operation that removes one,
  /// `#removeMethod` or `#removeLazySlot`.
  /// @param aBlock a one-argument block that stages an operation, an Array
  /// of the operation's Symbol and its text or name, through the builder,
  /// signalling what the builder's check signals.
  private class MutableMemberGroup adding: anAddSymbol removing: aRemoveSymbol staging: aBlock
      = Object (
    |
      /// The Symbol of the operation that adds or replaces a member.
      /// `addFromSource:` stages it with the member's text.
      private addOperation = anAddSymbol.
      /// The Symbol of the operation that removes a member.
      /// `removeMirrorNamed:` stages it with the member's name.
      private removeOperation = aRemoveSymbol.
      /// The block that stages an operation through the builder.
      /// Evaluated with one two-element Array per edit; it signals what
      /// the builder's check signals.
      private staging = aBlock.
    |
  ) (
    /// Stages the member `aString` declares: it replaces the member of the
    /// group's kind and of the same name the side declares or has staged,
    /// standing where that one stood, or is added last on the side when
    /// there is none.
    ///
    /// @param aString one member's text, a String or a Symbol, sent
    /// `asString`: one method declaration, `public foo: x = (^x)`, for a
    /// group of methods, one lazy slot declaration,
    /// `lazy public cache = 1.`, for a group of lazy slots.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic, staging nothing, for a text
    /// that does not parse ('<name>'s edited source does not parse: …
    /// (line <n>)'), one that declares no single member of the group's
    /// kind ('addFromSource: of <name>'s methods takes one method
    /// declaration', '… lazy slots takes one lazy slot declaration'), and a
    /// member that collides with a slot, a nested class, the factory or a
    /// member of another kind ('<name>'s edited source does not resolve: …
    /// (line <n>)').
    public addFromSource: aString = (
      staging value: {addOperation. aString asString}.
    )

    /// Stages the removal of the side's member of the group's kind named
    /// `aName`; a name the side neither declares nor has staged stages
    /// nothing and signals nothing. Another member's send to it never
    /// makes the check refuse: a send is bound late, and fails only when
    /// it runs.
    ///
    /// @param aName the member's name, a Symbol or a String, sent
    /// `asSymbol`.
    /// @answers the receiver.
    /// @signals Error with the VM's diagnostic, staging nothing, should the
    /// check refuse the declaration without the member.
    public removeMirrorNamed: aName = (
      staging value: {removeOperation. aName asSymbol}.
    )
  )

  /// Builds the facet `platform mirrors` answers. It is the module's one
  /// public member, named `build` like every shipped factory's.
  ///
  /// @answers a new `Mirrors` namespace.
  public build = (
    ^Mirrors new.
  )
)
